<PublicLayout title="About Tessellate" description="An open interface intelligence layer for people and agents."><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">A coherent product, not a pile of components</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">Describe a product, inspect its inferred architecture, compare three directions and edit a validated manifest in Workbench. Composition, audit and export run without an LLM.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Open and portable</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">The public resource source is free. Standalone exports contain React, TypeScript and Tailwind source without a Tessellate runtime dependency.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">This review version</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">Projects and collections are stored in your browser. Authentication, shared server persistence and community publishing require the canonical API deployment; this review does not pretend those services are connected.</p></section><p class="flex flex-wrap gap-5"><a class="underline" href="https://github.com/danishgm-sketch/Tessellate">Repository and contributions</a><a class="underline" href="/docs">Documentation</a><a class="underline" href="/explore">Inspect resource licences</a></p></PublicLayout>
